  v2 WSU data properties pipeline
  Brian Mason (NRAO)

  - rewrite (with claude code + codex) to be script-oriented, cleanly reconfigurable in assumptions, and testable

  Main pipeline

  - config.py
      - central configuration for WSU assumptions, milestone definitions, antenna/tint rules, and scenario knobs
      - also used by the ryanCy11 nchan analysis, though that workflow is otherwise separate
  - pipeline.py
      - main entry point for the Cy7/Cy8 data-properties statistics workflow
      - loads the per-MOUS ECSV database in data/, generates Band 1/2 realizations as needed, and computes projected M1/M4/M5 summary statistics
  - recompute.py
      - recomputes alternate WSU scenarios from an existing per-MOUS database
      - operates in memory on a loaded table, but the result can be written back out if desired
      - includes optional support for per-SPW nchan projection via wsu_projection.py, but the current Cy7/Cy8 DB does not itself contain per-SPW setup inputs
  - tables.py, plots.py
      - generate tables and plots from the pipeline/recompute outputs

  ryanCy11 nchan analysis

  - spw_tabulate.py
      - tabulates individual SPW characteristics (nchan, frequency, bandwidth, resolution, line-free fraction) from listobs and cont.dat
  - spw_setup_summary.py
      - summarizes the distribution of spectral setups and their characteristics
  - data directories:
      - ryanCy11 - raw input data
      - ryanCy11out - tabulated/intermediate products
      - ryanCy11wsu - WSU projection outputs from the ryanCy11 analysis
  - ryan_cy11_wsu_projection.py
      - runs the WSU projection comparison for the ryanCy11 sample
  - wsu_projection.py
      - shared helper code for projecting aggregate MOUS nchan from a current per-SPW setup under selectable projection logic
      - current supported modes:
          - memo_uniform_binned - original memo logic: all projected SPWs at one stepped2-binned resolution, based on the finest current SPW
          - memo_uniform_exact - same uniform-per-MOUS logic, but keep the exact finest current resolution instead of binning it
          - distributed_binned - preserve the current mix of SPW resolutions, but map each SPW into the stepped2 bins
          - distributed_exact - preserve the current mix of SPW resolutions using the exact current resolutions


